@.str.14 = private unnamed_addr constant [19 x i8] c"ScalableTSDFVolume\00", align 1
@.str.15 = private unnamed_addr constant [865 x i8] c"The\0AScalableTSDFVolume implements a more memory efficient data structure for\0Avolumetric integration.\0A\0AThis implementation is based on the following repository:\0Ahttps://github.com/qianyizh/ElasticReconstruction/tree/master/Integrate\0A\0AAn observed depth pixel gives two types of information: (a) an approximation\0Aof the nearby surface, and (b) empty space from the camera to the surface.\0AThey induce two core concepts of volumetric integration: weighted average of\0Aa truncated signed distance function (TSDF), and carving. The weighted\0Aaverage of TSDF is great in addressing the Gaussian noise along surface\0Anormal and producing a smooth surface output. The carving is great in\0Aremoving outlier structures like floating noise pixels and bumps along\0Astructure edges.\0A\0ARef: Dense Scene Reconstruction with Points of Interest\0A\0AQ.-Y. Zhou and V. Koltun\0A\0AIn SIGGRAPH, 2013\00", align 1
